---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: collections.watchVideos
  size: 1
  alias: video
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "/watch/{{ video.id }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ video.hostTitle }} (video)"
  description: "{{ video.description }}"
  ogImage: "/video/{{ video.id }}-poster.jpg"
  ogImageAlt: "A frame from the video on {{ video.hostTitle }}"
  ogImageSize: ""
---
{#- A watch page: the clip as the page's main content, which is what video
    search needs before it will index a video (lib/videos.js says why). The
    caption is the host page's own; nothing here is new text about the world,
    and the host page stays the clip's home. -#}
<script type="application/ld+json">{{ video | videoJsonLd(page.url, site.url, site.name) | safe }}</script>
<h1 class="page-title">{{ video.hostTitle }}</h1>
<video controls preload="metadata" poster="/star-rangers/video/{{ video.id }}-poster.jpg" style="width:100%;max-width:56rem;display:block;margin:1.5rem 0;background:#000">
  <source src="/star-rangers/video/{{ video.id }}.mp4" type="video/mp4">
  Your browser does not support the video element. <a href="/star-rangers/video/{{ video.id }}.mp4">Download the clip</a>.
</video>
<p class="page-intro"><em>{{ video.description }}</em></p>
<p>This video belongs to <a href="/star-rangers{{ video.page }}">{{ video.hostTitle }}</a>, which is where to read about it.</p>
